Benefits of App


- version control
    - see past versions of your work for any type of work—including microsoft word, apple notes, emails, music (logic pro)
    - compare changes that you made, including in microsoft word and apple notes
- share your work 
    - one source of truth, so your work you share is up to date
    - others don’t need the programs to view them 
    - send your work so others can find it without you knowing them beforehand
- command center
    - navigate through documents more easily
        - Mac sidebar helps when going between programs (eg, open apple notes when you are in chrome)
        - but if you are navigating between documents (eg, open one word document, when another word doc is in the foreground), it gets annoying
        - this makes that process easier
    - open new folders and create new documents, without having to minimize your windows
    - should be easier to create new files.
        - right now, you have to go to the program, open it, and then hit “new”.
        - better:
            - just create a button, and 
                - enter the extension (now—works for word, doesn’t work for some like .scpt files)
                - choose the file type (maybe later)
- easily put all your work for a project in one place
    - final product
    - drafts, 
    - research notes, 
    - feedback from others, 
    - online sources,
    - emails
    - audio, images, spreadsheets, and text data—
    - all together in one project place
    - so you can see everything at once
        - search everything
        - know what you need to keep track of
- elevate buttons: breathe big and gratitude notes
    - integrate the best way to feel, into your work
- all of this, without having to move your whole workflow into a new app, and house your data with a new app
    - you control all of it.
    - it is all still your work, your tools, your data
